     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The FDA-approved label for sertraline sets a maximum daily dose of 200 mg, so 1000 mg is not within it. I can't verify the claim, and it conflicts with what I know of the label.\n\nA 1000 mg dose would be a serious overdose for a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function. The risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the label range.** I can enter 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily right away.\n- **Get a pharmacist or attending to review it.** If there's a real reason for a dose above the label, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, they can verify it and document it. I can then enter the order with a note recording that approval.\n- **Check the source.** If the label text says otherwise, please send me the section. I'll look at it, but I can't enter the order on that basis alone.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
